# Local development. On a server this file is /opt/hikmah/.env, and the release
# rewrites it every deploy: it sets HIKMAH_DOMAIN, BETTER_AUTH_URL,
# HIKMAH_OWNER_EMAIL and BETTER_AUTH_SECRET from the Actions settings, generates
# HIKMAH_VAULT_KEY, HIKMAH_SEARCH_SECRET and HIKMAH_WORKBENCH_TOKEN once, and
# carries every other KEY=VALUE line through untouched. So a Stripe, Resend,
# Google or provider key you set there by hand survives — it did not until
# recently, which is why none of them could be configured in production.
#
# Comments are not carried through, and a value with a space or a '#' should be
# quoted: compose's dotenv parser, not this file, decides how it is read.

BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000
# Generate a new secret locally: openssl rand -hex 32
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=REPLACE_WITH_A_RANDOM_SECRET
HIKMAH_OWNER_EMAIL=owner@example.com
# Use an absolute path in production. Docker sets /data.
HIKMAH_DATA_DIR=.data
# The execution sidecar. Signs single-use terminal tickets and authenticates the
# app to the workbench, so both services must hold the same value.
# Generate: openssl rand -hex 32 — configure.py does this for you on a server.
HIKMAH_WORKBENCH_TOKEN=REPLACE_WITH_A_RANDOM_SECRET
HIKMAH_WORKBENCH_URL=http://localhost:3001

# Registration is closed by default (v10): a self-hosted workspace holding the
# owner's provider keys must not depend on remembering a flag. Set this on a
# deployment that should let anyone sign up:
# HIKMAH_PUBLIC=1
# (HIKMAH_PRIVATE=1 still forces closed for explicitness.)

# Transactional email, through Resend. Without both of these the app still runs,
# but addresses are not verified and there is no password reset, so a customer
# who forgets their password has no way back in. Set them before taking money.
# Create a key at resend.com and verify the sending domain first.
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# HIKMAH_MAIL_FROM=Hikmah <hello@your-domain.example>

# Sign in with Google. Both or neither: with neither, the button is not shown
# rather than shown and failing. Create an OAuth client in Google Cloud with the
# redirect URI <BETTER_AUTH_URL>/api/auth/callback/google.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Payments, through Stripe. Without these the pricing page shows the plans and
# says checkout is not configured, rather than offering a button that 500s. The
# webhook endpoint is <BETTER_AUTH_URL>/api/auth/stripe/webhook.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# STRIPE_PRICE_PRO=
# STRIPE_PRICE_PRO_ANNUAL=

# A provider key for the whole deployment, used when a run carries no saved key
# of its own. Owners normally set theirs under Settings -> Connection in the
# chat instead, which keeps it encrypted in the database rather than in the
# environment. Without either, a run against a hosted provider is refused with
# that reason rather than queued and failed.
# HIKMAH_PROVIDER_KEY=

# A model server on this machine or the private network — Ollama, vLLM, any
# OpenAI-compatible endpoint. The app refuses non-public hosts unless they are
# named here, comma-separated, host or host:port. Ollama on the Docker host:
# HIKMAH_PROVIDER_ALLOW_PRIVATE=host.docker.internal
# then choose "Ollama (local)" under Settings -> Connection in the chat and
# set the endpoint to http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1. Loopback needs no
# entry: an app run outside Docker reaches http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1 as is.

# Image and speech generation, which go through OpenRouter. Leave this unset
# when the workspace already runs on OpenRouter: a run's own key is used, so
# media needs no second credential. Set it only to generate media while chatting
# through some other provider. Without either, the media tools are not offered
# rather than offered and failing on every call.
# HIKMAH_MEDIA_KEY=
# Which models to generate with, when neither the owner nor the model names one.
# HIKMAH_IMAGE_MODEL=openai/gpt-image-1
# HIKMAH_SPEECH_MODEL=openai/gpt-4o-mini-tts
# HIKMAH_SPEECH_VOICE=alloy

# How many runs the worker drives at once. Two by default: a chat and, beside
# it, one background task. The last slot always goes to a chat, so a task never
# makes a conversation wait.
# HIKMAH_RUN_CONCURRENCY=2
